Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:25:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Input: stmpe-keypad - add an OF match table

The STMPE MFD core creates the keypad cell with the "st,stmpe-keypad"
compatible, so the platform device has an OF node and its uevent only
carries the OF modalias. The driver matches by name and has no module
aliases at all, so a modular build is never loaded automatically.

Add an OF match table with MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE.

Seen with an STMPE1801 keypad on the Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 keyboard
cover: the keypad cell appeared, but the input device only after a
manual modprobe.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/input/keyboard/stmpe-keypad.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/stmpe-keypad.c b/drivers/input/keyboard/stmpe-keypad.c
index 988fd4045b..c6f54bf4e3 100644
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/stmpe-keypad.c
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/stmpe-keypad.c
@@ -724,8 +724,17 @@ static void stmpe_keypad_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	stmpe_keypad_stop(&stmpe_keypad_lifecycle_ops, keypad);
 }
 
+static const struct of_device_id stmpe_keypad_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "st,stmpe-keypad" },
+	{ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, stmpe_keypad_of_match);
+
 static struct platform_driver stmpe_keypad_driver = {
-	.driver.name	= "stmpe-keypad",
+	.driver = {
+		.name		= "stmpe-keypad",
+		.of_match_table	= stmpe_keypad_of_match,
+	},
 	.probe		= stmpe_keypad_probe,
 	.remove		= stmpe_keypad_remove,
 };
